<title>CANADA: Canada new housing price index rises in April.</title>
<headline>Canada new housing price index rises in April.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's new housing price index rose 0.8 percent in April to 132.7 (base 1986) from April 1996, Statistics Canada said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>    Index			 April     yr pct  month pct</p>
<p> Total			    132.7     +0.8	+0.2</p>
<p> House only		     122.9     +1.5	+0.2</p>
<p> Land only			165.3     -0.2	 nil</p>
<p>The index measures changes of contractors' selling prices of new residential houses.</p>
<p>A Reuter survey of economists had forecast a 0.2 percent rise in the annual index.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613-235-6745))</p>
</text>
